{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791822297,"nonce":"Tu2U0uUaCb67BBb17vlp/BKQpDM=","title":"Repeated SignalString reads allocate while the value is unchanged","message":"The editor render-path check exposed allocations decoding a native string on every SignalString.get(). SignalString.get calls Utf8.decode(blinc_signal_get_string(ptr)); String.fromUTF8 creates Haxe storage even when the native value has not changed. The concrete source path establishes this is a conversion cost, independent of interface dispatch.\n\nReproducer in the sibling ChimpMonk checkout: repro/ashui_signal_reads/Repro.hx. From ChimpMonk root:\n  haxe -cp repro/ashui_signal_reads -cp example/src -cp ../ashui/haxe -hl editor/bin/signal-read-repro.hl -main Repro\n  ../ash/target/release/ash --preset application editor/bin/signal-read-repro.hl\nStage the existing AshUI blinc_abi library into editor/bin as scripts/editor.sh does.\n\nOn this Mac, warmed 8,192 reads report nativeString=524208 bytes and haxeString=0. The alternative uses the existing SignalDynamic\u003cString\u003e, which keeps the Haxe value and touches a native revision to track dependencies. The editor uses that for its frame-read primary selection.\n\nOpportunity: cache the decoded Haxe string by native revision while preserving dependency registration, native writes, null handling and identical-value semantics. A check must prove repeated unchanged reads allocate zero and native value changes remain visible. This entry concerns string decoding; generic integer interface boxing is separately reported to Ash.","files":null}]}